    "problem": "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}$?",
    "worked_solution": "Let $A$ denote the given matrix. Expand along the third column. Terms with a zero entry vanish. The cofactor signs are $(-1)^{i+j}$.\n\n$$\n\\det(A)=-5(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+1(-1)^{4+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the smaller determinants gives\n\n$$\n\\det(A)=109.\n$$",
